From 4f4a20b5a24edc82c20a4d469ab14d1a5f582d41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:49:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] common: define the native AROS platform baseline [angle]
 [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: ANGLE rejected the AROS compiler target before defining any OS family. That also suppressed its POSIX GCC bit-scan overloads, producing secondary ambiguous-call failures throughout common math code.

FIX_REASON: Define ANGLE_PLATFORM_AROS and the POSIX baseline while deliberately not defining ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX. This enables portable compiler and threading primitives without claiming Linux-only loaders, filesystems, or window systems.

SCOPE: ANGLE common platform detection.

VALIDATION: PackedEGLEnums_autogen.o, MemoryBuffer.o, Float16ToFloat32.o, and PackedEnums.o compile in the filtered AROS headless graph.

RISK: medium; ANGLE_PLATFORM_POSIX exposes later facility-level assumptions that must be adapted explicitly when encountered.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 src/common/platform.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/common/platform.h b/src/common/platform.h
index 1184891..df469d3 100644
--- a/src/common/platform.h
+++ b/src/common/platform.h
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@
 #elif defined(ANDROID)
 #    define ANGLE_PLATFORM_ANDROID 1
 #    define ANGLE_PLATFORM_POSIX 1
+#elif defined(__AROS__)
+#    define ANGLE_PLATFORM_AROS 1
+#    define ANGLE_PLATFORM_POSIX 1
 #elif defined(__ggp__)
 #    define ANGLE_PLATFORM_GGP 1
 #    define ANGLE_PLATFORM_POSIX 1
